═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 TOKEN FLOW EXAMPLE: 4,600-line COBOL program (TURBO profile)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

 File: 4600LoC.cbl  │  ~150K chars  │  ~50K estimated tokens
                     │
 ① Triage:           LARGE (> MaxChunkSize)
                     │
 ② Smart Chunk:      Split into 4 chunks at paragraph boundaries
                     │
                     ├── Chunk 1: IDENTIFICATION + DATA DIVISION    ~12K tokens
                     ├── Chunk 2: PROCEDURE (paragraphs A-M)        ~15K tokens
                     ├── Chunk 3: PROCEDURE (paragraphs N-Z)        ~13K tokens
                     └── Chunk 4: ERROR HANDLING + CLEANUP          ~10K tokens
                     │
 ③ Complexity:       Score = 18 (EXEC SQL + EXEC CICS + REDEFINES)
                     → HIGH tier → reasoning: "high", output: 100K
                     │
 ④ Parallel:         3 chunk workers, 2000ms stagger
                     │
                     │  t=0.0s  Chunk 1 starts ──► WaitForCapacity(12K) ──► ✅
                     │  t=2.0s  Chunk 2 starts ──► WaitForCapacity(15K) ──► ✅
                     │  t=4.0s  Chunk 3 starts ──► WaitForCapacity(13K) ──► ✅
                     │  t=6.0s  Chunk 4 waits  ──► semaphore (max 3)
                     │  t=35s   Chunk 1 done   ──► RecordUsage(48K actual)
                     │          Chunk 4 starts ──► WaitForCapacity(10K) ──► ✅
                     │
 ⑤ Sliding Window:   At t=35s window shows:
                     │  Chunk 1: 48K + Chunk 2: ~55K (in-flight) = ~103K
                     │  103K < 210K budget ──► still has capacity
                     │
 ⑥ Reconcile:        All 4 chunks done → validate cross-references
                     → type mappings consistent ✅
                     → all signatures resolved ✅
                     │
 ⑦ Output:           Single coherent Java/C# filelogs/
